pcs-rtl-otto: select HSGMII on a 2500BASE-X lane via realtek,hisgmii

HSGMII (HiSGMII, rate-adapting 2.5G SGMII) and clause-37 2500BASE-X share
the 3.125 GBaud line rate, the analog setup, the CMU page, the PLL speed and
the TX config on this SerDes.  The only thing that differs is the mode value
programmed into the lane: 0x12 instead of 0x16.

That is a PCS-internal hardware detail, not a distinct MAC-PHY interface, so
express it as a per-lane vendor property rather than a new phy_interface_t.
Boards keep the standard phy-mode = "2500base-x" and mark the lane:

	serdes@7 {
		reg = <7>;
		realtek,hisgmii;
	};

Doing it the other way - a PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_HSGMII of our own - meant
patching four core kernel files and adding a HISGMII case to every switch
over the mode enum.  It broke twice: once when 6.18 moved the enum and the
interface->capability table, and once when upstream added a new switch
(rtpcs_93xx_sds_get_cmu_page()) that our patch knew nothing about, which
silently dropped the CR1000A's MoCA link to 1G.  Riding on 2500BASE-X means
upstream's own cases cover the mode for free.

The property is only meaningful on RTL93xx; other families never set it, so
their behaviour is unchanged.

--- a/pcs-rtl-otto.c
+++ b/pcs-rtl-otto.c
@@ -120,6 +120,7 @@
 #define RTPCS_93XX_SDS_MODE_QSGMII		0x06
 #define RTPCS_93XX_SDS_MODE_USXGMII		0x0d
 #define RTPCS_93XX_SDS_MODE_XSGMII		0x10
+#define RTPCS_93XX_SDS_MODE_HISGMII		0x12
 #define RTPCS_93XX_SDS_MODE_2500BASEX		0x16
 #define RTPCS_93XX_SDS_MODE_10GBASER		0x1a
 #define RTPCS_93XX_SDS_MODE_OFF			0x1f
@@ -439,6 +440,7 @@
 	u8 num_of_links;
 	bool first_start;
 	bool skip_rx_cali;	/* board quirk: skip the loopback RX-cal on this lane */
+	bool hisgmii;		/* 2.5G lane runs HSGMII, not clause-37 2500BASE-X */
 	const u32 *fwnode_overrides;	/* <page reg mask value> quadruplets */
 	int n_fwnode_overrides;
 };
@@ -901,6 +903,8 @@
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	val = cfg->sds_hw_mode_vals[hw_mode];
+	if (sds->hisgmii && hw_mode == RTPCS_SDS_MODE_2500BASEX)
+		val = RTPCS_93XX_SDS_MODE_HISGMII;
 	if (val < 0)
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 
@@ -1807,6 +1811,8 @@
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	raw = sds->ctrl->cfg->sds_hw_mode_vals[hw_mode];
+	if (sds->hisgmii && hw_mode == RTPCS_SDS_MODE_2500BASEX)
+		raw = RTPCS_93XX_SDS_MODE_HISGMII;
 	if (raw < 0)
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 
@@ -4631,6 +4637,8 @@
 		sds->skip_rx_cali =
 			fwnode_property_present(sds->fwnode,
 						"realtek,skip-rx-calibration");
+		sds->hisgmii = fwnode_property_present(sds->fwnode,
+						       "realtek,hisgmii");
 		ret = rtpcs_sds_parse_fwnode_overrides(dev, sds);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
